Primitive Datatypes
byte, short, int, long, float, double, char, boolean
PRIMITIVE
byte	1 byte	Stores small integer values	byte a = 10;
short	2 bytes	Stores short integer values	short b = 1000;
int	4 bytes	Stores integer values	int c = 50000;
long	8 bytes	Stores large integer values	long d = 123456L;
float	4 bytes	Stores decimal values	float e = 10.5f;
double	8 bytes	Stores large decimal values	double f = 25.567;
char	2 bytes	Stores a single character	char g = 'A';

Non-primitive Datatypes
String, Array, Class, Object, Interface

